  "body": "Fixes #7766\n\n`count_periods`' `Period::Custom` branch used unchecked `i64` arithmetic on a peer-supplied `anchor` (`body.rs` rejects only a zero length). Extreme anchors panicked in debug builds and silently wrapped to phantom or end-before-start windows in release builds.\n\nThis change uses `checked_sub` / `checked_mul` / `checked_add` for the index, start, end, and previous-window start, returning `EvalError::OutOfRange` on overflow — the same ruling the Day/Week branches get from the calendar.\n\nVerification (laptop, worktree on current main):\n- New regression test `custom_period_extreme_anchor_is_out_of_range_not_a_panic_or_wrapped_window` covers anchor `i64::MIN`, anchor near `i64::MAX` (end overflow), and a previous-window underflow, plus an ordinary-period control. It fails on the pre-fix code and passes with the fix.\n- `cargo test --lib didit::` — 28 passed, 0 failed.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796751331&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7769&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7769&signature=70fdb8f7865076e4c38d5335e3688df50ffa6a6e55e01a1030813f704656ed56\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7769?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->",
